Z||000000||sqoach||11-12-2001||02:17 PM||||Those darn little critters are everywhere!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> We've caught like 6 in the past 24 hours! I bet the leaves all over the place don't help. Plus we have an old house. Anyone else having a mouse problem? What are you doing to get rid of them?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||11
Z||000001||JSocha||11-12-2001||02:36 PM||||Break out the canoe and setup your fall trapping line of mouse traps!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||FieroFanaticus2||11-12-2001||02:40 PM||||Get a couple of Cats||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brian87egotrip||11-12-2001||02:48 PM||||I should of known you would reply Jsocha.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I had rats real bad earlier this year.  Lots of traps and a cat. took about two months to get rid of them. My wife and I wouldn't sleep at home either. Nasty little creatures.<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Return of Fiero||11-12-2001||03:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroFanaticus2:<BR><B>Get a couple of Cats</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My cat played with the mice, and a few times i woke up with the cat sleeping with the mice (also sleeping)<P>Myke||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||11-12-2001||03:34 PM||||Be careful with the chemical rodent killers. The rat eats the bait and then crawls to some inaccessible location of your house to die and stink the whole place up and breed flies.<P>Edited because I forgot how to spell flies and did not want to be arrested by the grammar police  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||JSocha||11-12-2001||03:40 PM||||You have to remember, that the "Grammer Policeman" PFF had, has been booted off the PFF island.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  hehehehe||||reg||10
Z||000007||fogglethorpe||11-12-2001||05:12 PM||||Get one of those one-way trap door devices, and smear peanut butter in it as bait. This has worked for me in the past, and it's less messy. (I believe in being humane before I take them outside and smash them with bricks).||||reg||1
Z||000008||avengador1||11-12-2001||06:37 PM||||You could try the sticky traps. At least when you catch them they will be where you can find them. I had one in the garage for a week and the little pig ate all the poison baits. I had to buy more and he finaly croaked. Luckily he decided to die in plain view so I could find him.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||11-12-2001||07:35 PM||||Get a .22 caliber and a box of ratshot.  It can get a bit messy but its lots of fun!||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||11-12-2001||07:49 PM||||Egad! 2 more already! We're using two of the more popular types mouse traps. *Thwack!*<BR>I kinda wish we didn't have to kill them, but they're un-invited guests, and we don't have any other way of getting rid of them. We use to have one of those trap-door traps, but it didn't work as good. And can't get any cats, my dog hates 'em. He goes crazy every time he hears the word, CAT!<BR>Maybe we could get a small snake a turn him loose!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierowrecker||11-12-2001||08:59 PM||||Hey Squoash!<BR>Get a few boxes of moth balls and spread them in the basement/crawl space, and in the attic...<BR>Also put them in cupboards under sinks...<BR>Works on rats, mice, squirels, skunks and bats...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000012||JSocha||11-12-2001||09:48 PM||||Get a Ferret.  Then when he is done catching all the mice, give your dog a treat!<P>Nobody here seen me write this...now did they?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||jeffreyeffrey||11-14-2001||04:36 PM||||a couple of years ago when I was in college our apartment was lousy with mice. The sticky traps worked the best we caught 5 the first night. Only bad part is they are alive of coarse when you come across them. we just took the whole trap down and tossed'em in the dumpster.||||reg||1
Z||000014||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-14-2001||06:44 PM||||We moved last fall to my family home in the country that was left empty for a few years,  we had mice and rats, After we remodeled inside, and took our 5 indoor cats there, we soon got rid of the mice,(our cats wont eat them, just holds them until we take them away and dispose of them) but the rats were outdoor, One day I opened the fiero trunk and a rat was sitting by my manifold..  It didnt take me long to stake out them b@stards with a 12gauge before they started chewing wires up on our cars..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I heard that mice reproduce every 2 weeks, so you want to make sure you get them soon.. <P>basic traps are best in my eyes, but be sure to wear gloves when disposing of the traps/mice<P>Good luck!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||sqoach||11-14-2001||08:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>Get a Ferret.  Then when he is done catching all the mice, give your dog a treat!<P>Nobody here seen me write this...now did they?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Haha! That sure would be an expensive dog treat!<BR>We haven't seen or caught any mice for the past 36 hours. Of course they might have gotten smart and moved to a different part of the house. At least there's no more in the laundry room...I hope  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">||||reg||1
